<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore parliament dissolved ahead of elections.</title>
<headline>Singapore parliament dissolved ahead of elections.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Ong Teng Cheong dissolved the Singapore parliament on Monday, the government said, setting the stage for general elections expected to be held in the next few weeks.</p>
<p>The government announcement did not say when the elections would be, but Prime Minister Goh Chok Tong suggested at the weekend he expected to name dates after next Sunday.</p>
</text>
